<article class="env-lemma" id="0D2V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D2V">Lemma <span data-tag="0D2V">69.16.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a Noetherian algebraic space over $S$. Assume that for every coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$ we have $H^1(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$. Then $X$ is an affine scheme. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption implies that $H^1(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for every quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$ by Lemmas <a href="/tag/07UV" data-tag="07UV">69.15.1</a> and <a href="/tag/073E" data-tag="073E">69.5.1</a>. Then $X$ is affine by Proposition <a href="/tag/07V6" data-tag="07V6">69.16.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>